{"status":"ready","content":"I need to compute the sample variance of the given data set.\r\n\r\nGiven data: {9, 14, 5, 4, -20, -13, -5, 13}\r\n\r\nStep 1: Find the sample mean (x̄).\r\nNumber of data points: n = 8\r\n\r\nSum = 9 + 14 + 5 + 4 + (-20) + (-13) + (-5) + 13\r\nSum = 9 + 14 + 5 + 4 - 20 - 13 - 5 + 13\r\nSum = 7\r\n\r\nSample mean: x̄ = 7/8\r\n\r\nStep 2: Calculate the squared deviations from the mean.\r\nFor each data point xi, calculate (xi - x̄)²:\r\n\r\n- (9 - 7/8)² = (72/8 - 7/8)² = (65/8)² = 4225/64\r\n- (14 - 7/8)² = (112/8 - 7/8)² = (105/8)² = 11025/64\r\n- (5 - 7/8)² = (40/8 - 7/8)² = (33/8)² = 1089/64\r\n- (4 - 7/8)² = (32/8 - 7/8)² = (25/8)² = 625/64\r\n- (-20 - 7/8)² = (-160/8 - 7/8)² = (-167/8)² = 27889/64\r\n- (-13 - 7/8)² = (-104/8 - 7/8)² = (-111/8)² = 12321/64\r\n- (-5 - 7/8)² = (-40/8 - 7/8)² = (-47/8)² = 2209/64\r\n- (13 - 7/8)² = (104/8 - 7/8)² = (97/8)² = 9409/64\r\n\r\nStep 3: Sum the squared deviations.\r\nSum = 4225/64 + 11025/64 + 1089/64 + 625/64 + 27889/64 + 12321/64 + 2209/64 + 9409/64\r\nSum = (4225 + 11025 + 1089 + 625 + 27889 + 12321 + 2209 + 9409)/64\r\nSum = 68792/64\r\n\r\nStep 4: Calculate the sample variance.\r\nSample variance = Sum of squared deviations / (n - 1)\r\nSample variance = (68792/64) / 7\r\nSample variance = 68792/(64 × 7)\r\nSample variance = 68792/448\r\n\r\nStep 5: Simplify the fraction.\r\nFind GCD of 68792 and 448:\r\n68792 = 448 × 153 + 248\r\n448 = 248 × 1 + 200\r\n248 = 200 × 1 + 48\r\n200 = 48 × 4 + 8\r\n48 = 8 × 6 + 0\r\n\r\nGCD = 8\r\n\r\n68792 ÷ 8 = 8599\r\n448 ÷ 8 = 56\r\n\r\nTherefore: 68792/448 = 8599/56\r\n\r\n$\\boxed{\\frac{8599}{56}}$\r\n","path":"responses/claude-opus-4/livebench-052-math.txt","size":1544,"mtime":1779365165}